traceability.evidence:
Story file exists and matches the assessed spec:
- docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md (verified via read_file).,Implementation of JSDoc coexistence, boundary detection, and continuation logic in the valid-annotation-format rule:
- src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts
  - normalizeCommentLine(rawLine: string):
    - Trims, strips leading '*' for non-traceability lines, preserves per-line boundaries rather than concatenating multiple lines.
    - Keeps annotation tags and other content on the same line only:
      ```ts
      const trimmed = rawLine.trim();
      if (!trimmed) return "";
      const filtered = trimmed.replace(/`[^`]*`/g, (match) => " ".repeat(match.length));
      const annotationMatch = filtered.match(/@story\b|@req\b|@supports\b/);
      if (!annotationMatch || annotationMatch.index === undefined) {
        const withoutLeadingStar = filtered.replace(/^\*\s?/, "");
        return withoutLeadingStar;
      }
      return filtered.slice(annotationMatch.index);
      ```
    - This avoids cross-line concatenation and is compatible with multi-line annotations.
  - isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string):
    - Detects any non-traceability JSDoc tag line as a boundary:
      ```ts
      export function isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string): boolean {
        const trimmed = normalized.trimStart();
        if (!trimmed || !trimmed.startsWith("@")) {
          return false;
        }
        if (/^@(story|req|supports)\b/.test(trimmed)) {
          return false;
        }
        return true;
      }
      ```
    - This matches any `@word` other than @story/@req/@supports, fulfilling REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION and contributing to REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE.

- src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts
  - processCommentLine(...) wires JSDoc coexistence into the main parsing flow:
    ```ts
    const isStory = /@story\b/.test(normalized);
    const isReq = /@req\b/.test(normalized);
    const isImplements = /@supports\b/.test(normalized);
    // ... @supports handled as single-line
    if (isStory || isReq) {
      finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
      const value = normalized.replace(/^@story\b|^@req\b/, "").trim();
      return {
        type: isStory ? "story" : "req",
        value,
        hasValue: value.trim().length > 0,
      };
    }

    // Implement JSDoc tag coexistence behavior: terminate @story/@req values when a new non-traceability JSDoc tag line (e.g., @param, @returns) is encountered.
    // @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
    if (isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized)) {
      finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
      return null;
    }

    if (pending) {
      const continuation = normalized.trim();
      if (!continuation) {
        return pending;
      }
      const updatedValue = pending.value
        ? `${pending.value} ${continuation}`
        : continuation;
      return {
        ...pending,
        value: updatedValue,
        hasValue: pending.hasValue || continuation.length > 0,
      };
    }
    ```
  - Effects:
    - Any non-traceability JSDoc tag line (e.g. @param, @returns, @throws) immediately finalizes the current @story/@req pending value (REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION, REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION).
    - Such lines are never treated as continuation lines for a pending traceability annotation, satisfying REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC.
    - @supports remains a single-line parse that does not interfere with multi-line story/req handling, preserving behavior from dependencies 005.0 and 010.2 (Backward Compatible).

